>> title: Cuban Black Beans
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: beans, cuban, sofrito, stovetop
>> counters: Taquería, One Pot
>> aka: frijoles negros, black beans
>> servings: 6
>> time: 2 hr 15 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the vinegar goes in at the very end: acid in with beans that are not yet soft sets the skins, and no simmering takes it back

>> step: simmer 1 1/2 hr
Simmer @dried black beans{1%lb}(450 g; soaked overnight) in @water{8%cups}(1.9 L) with @bay leaves{2} until tender, ~{1 1/2%hr}.

>> step: sweat 10 min
Sweat @green bell pepper{1%large}, @yellow onion{1%large}, and @garlic{5%cloves} in @olive oil{1/4%cup}(60 mL) in a #skillet{} for ~{10%min}.

>> step: toast 1 min
Toast @&(~1)sofrito{} with @ground cumin{1 1/2%tsp} and @dried oregano{1%tsp} for ~{1%min}.

>> step: simmer 30 min
Stir @&(~1)sofrito{} into @&(~3)beans{} and simmer uncovered for ~{30%min}, until the broth is thick.

>> step: season, pull the bay leaves
Season @&(~1)beans{} with @dry white wine{2%Tbs}, @cider vinegar{1%Tbs}, and @kosher salt{2%tsp}, then pull the bay leaves.
